  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Navigation: distance along the equator</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.7 (c) / Essential 2.3 (d): Find the shorter distance between two points on the equator in nautical miles and kilometres.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 3 (The sphere), Section 6, Example 1 and Exercise D, question 3 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: distance along the equator the shorter way round; new longitudes.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
